KingMod

Build the x64 Release configuration with Visual Studio C++ and Windows SDK.
The project uses C++20 and toolset v145 for Release (v143 for Debug).
Install vcpkg and integrate it with MSBuild, or set VcpkgRoot explicitly.
Required x64-windows-static packages: curl, openssl, zlib, detours, minhook.
Bundled FreeType and Discord RPC libraries are retained as build dependencies.

Build KingMod and RocketSim together:
  msbuild KingMod.sln /p:Configuration=Release /p:Platform=x64 /m

RocketSim is a project dependency and is compiled automatically from source.
No manually downloaded RocketSim.lib is required.
The optional standalone CMake build remains available:
  cmake -S RocketSim -B RocketSim/build -A x64
  cmake --build RocketSim/build --config Release

Optional standalone injector:
  cmake -S . -B build-injector -A x64
  cmake --build build-injector --config Release

KingMod runs without a license key or authentication server.
Third-party notices are retained in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES and vendor license files.

Public builds ship without personal Discord IDs or signing keys.
Set KINGMOD_DISCORD_APPLICATION_ID and KINGMOD_PSYNET_SIGNING_KEY through
compiler definitions when these optional integrations are needed.
Their defaults are empty, which disables Discord RPC and response signing.
